results.answer:
The briefing said the independent evaluation found that:

- the pilot exceeded its target of 1,500 registered borrowers;
- use grew in the second year;
- borrowers reported saving money;
- most items were returned in good condition.

It also noted one disagreement with the evaluation: the library service said its own repair log showed damage on 6.8% of loans, which it regarded as a better measure of wear and tear than the evaluation’s figure.

ANSWER: The main findings were that the pilot beat its registration target, usage increased in year two, borrowers saved money, and most items were returned in good condition; the service only disputed the damage rate, saying its repair log showed 6.8% of loans had damage.
